{
 "family": "select",
 "note": "Rulings Q9 to Q13 for the selection of internal/cleanup. Q9: an asset has a repository, a path, the coordinates group, name and version (empty where it has none), the time its blob was last updated (blobCreated), the last download time this server recorded (lastDownloaded) and the last download time an import brought (importedLastDownloaded), the last two absent when there is none. The selection also takes the build time of the catalog file (catalogBuilt) and the current time (now), given for the file and replaced by a case that names its own. Times are RFC 3339; a time with an offset is the same instant in UTC. Q10 (decision A19): the value of the last download is the latest of the recorded time, the imported time and the build time of the catalog file; the key lastDownload of an asset is the value the case expects. Q11: an asset is selected when every criterion that is set holds; lastBlobUpdatedDays N holds when the blob was last updated more than N days before now, lastDownloadedDays N when the value of Q10 lies more than N days before now; a day is 24 hours, a time exactly N days back does not hold, and an absent or null criterion is not applied. Q12: for criteria that admin.Runnable refuses, nothing is selected, runnable is false and unknown names the criteria of another name; the selection never falls back to the known criteria of such a policy. Q13: the selected assets are sorted by path in byte order; the preview holds the first 100 as items (repository, group, name, version, path), total counts all, and truncated is true when total is above 100. The key selected lists the paths the case selects, in order; selectedCount gives their number where the case generates its assets. A key repeat of an asset expands it into that many assets, numbered from the last one down: {n} in its path, name and version becomes 100, 099 and so on to 000 for 101 assets, so that the input is not in the order of the paths. The key preview states total and truncated, and the items in full or their count with the first and the last path. Every case runs twice, with the numbers of the criteria decoded as float64 and as json.Number. The repositories, paths and times are invented.",
